cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Survival of the Anschlussfähigsten: Eine operational-formale Übertragung des evolutionären Fitnessgedankens auf Computer-, Informations- und soziotechnische Systeme"
message: "Please cite the future versioned Zenodo record associated with these exact files. No DOI or release date is embedded in this prepublication bundle."
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Lohmann
    given-names: Ingolf
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher; QIK-VRT"
version: "1.0.0-candidate"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Goldkelch/qik-vrt"
abstract: >-
  A scoped computer-science interpretation of survival of the fittest as
  survival of the most connectable. The work distinguishes biological fitness,
  authorial interpretation, formal transition-system theorems and empirical
  applicability. Its Lean source models finite operational continuation through
  viable connections; its five formal claims are bound by a successful H2/H3
  exact-head kernel receipt. No empirical survival effect is claimed as proved.
keywords:
  - QIK-VRT
  - connectability
  - operational continuation
  - viability
  - transition systems
  - formal verification
  - Lean
  - evolution
